1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,214
Little Moments.

2
00:00:02,214 --> 00:00:04,755
One More, Please!

3
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:09,605
It's Saturday morning, and the bakery smells amazing.

4
00:00:09,605 --> 00:00:11,467
Warm bread.

5
00:00:11,467 --> 00:00:13,586
Sweet cinnamon.

6
00:00:13,586 --> 00:00:15,910
And something buttery.

7
00:00:15,910 --> 00:00:18,423
Dad smiles at me.

8
00:00:18,423 --> 00:00:21,494
You're ordering today, Lucy.

9
00:00:21,494 --> 00:00:22,866
Me?

10
00:00:22,866 --> 00:00:24,225
Yep.

11
00:00:24,225 --> 00:00:26,358
I'll be right here.

12
00:00:26,358 --> 00:00:27,839
Okay.

13
00:00:27,839 --> 00:00:29,918
I can do this.

14
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:33,260
The woman behind the counter waves.

15
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:34,945
Hi there!

16
00:00:34,945 --> 00:00:37,255
What can I get for you?

17
00:00:37,255 --> 00:00:41,032
Could I have two cinnamon rolls, please?

18
00:00:41,032 --> 00:00:42,499
Sure!

19
00:00:42,499 --> 00:00:44,823
For here or to go?

20
00:00:44,823 --> 00:00:46,915
I look at Dad.

21
00:00:46,915 --> 00:00:50,298
He points to the little paper bags.

22
00:00:50,298 --> 00:00:52,608
To go, please.

23
00:00:52,608 --> 00:00:55,543
The woman reaches for a bag.

24
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:59,388
Then I remember my little brother, Ben.

25
00:00:59,388 --> 00:01:04,877
He's at home, probably asking Mom when breakfast is coming.

26
00:01:04,877 --> 00:01:08,220
Actually, could we make that three?

27
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:10,040
Of course.

28
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:12,648
Three cinnamon rolls.

29
00:01:12,648 --> 00:01:15,366
Dad raises an eyebrow.

30
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:17,961
Who's the third one for?

31
00:01:17,961 --> 00:01:19,415
Ben!

32
00:01:19,415 --> 00:01:21,277
Good thinking.

33
00:01:21,277 --> 00:01:25,597
He'd notice if we came home smelling like cinnamon.

34
00:01:25,597 --> 00:01:27,296
I laugh.

35
00:01:27,296 --> 00:01:32,214
Then I spot a tray of tiny cookies shaped like cats.

36
00:01:32,214 --> 00:01:34,796
One has a crooked ear.

37
00:01:34,796 --> 00:01:38,519
It looks a little like our cat, Noodle.

38
00:01:38,519 --> 00:01:40,557
Dad, look!

39
00:01:40,557 --> 00:01:42,785
That one's Noodle.

40
00:01:42,785 --> 00:01:45,244
It does look like him.

41
00:01:45,244 --> 00:01:47,975
Can we get a cookie, too?

42
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:50,366
Dad checks the bag.

43
00:01:50,366 --> 00:01:53,315
Let's stick with the rolls today.

44
00:01:53,315 --> 00:01:54,796
Okay.

45
00:01:54,796 --> 00:01:57,038
Maybe next time.

46
00:01:57,038 --> 00:02:00,298
The woman hands me our breakfast.

47
00:02:00,298 --> 00:02:02,214
How much is it?

48
00:02:02,214 --> 00:02:05,108
Nine dollars, please.

49
00:02:05,108 --> 00:02:08,532
Dad pays, and I take the bag.

50
00:02:08,532 --> 00:02:11,657
It's warm against my fingers.

51
00:02:11,657 --> 00:02:15,135
Could we have a few napkins, please?

52
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,105
Absolutely.

53
00:02:17,105 --> 00:02:18,913
Here you go.

54
00:02:18,913 --> 00:02:20,584
Thank you!

55
00:02:20,584 --> 00:02:22,676
Have a nice day!

56
00:02:22,676 --> 00:02:24,592
You, too!

57
00:02:24,592 --> 00:02:27,675
Outside, Dad grins.

58
00:02:27,675 --> 00:02:30,570
You handled that really well.

59
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:32,595
I grin back.

60
00:02:32,595 --> 00:02:36,725
I only forgot Ben for about three seconds.

61
00:02:36,725 --> 00:02:40,203
At home, Ben runs to the door.

62
00:02:40,203 --> 00:02:42,527
Did you get me anything?

63
00:02:42,527 --> 00:02:44,875
I hold up the bag.

64
00:02:44,875 --> 00:02:47,269
One cinnamon roll.

65
00:02:47,269 --> 00:02:49,225
Just for you.

66
00:02:49,225 --> 00:02:51,277
You're the best!

67
00:02:51,277 --> 00:02:54,904
Noodle walks over and sniffs the bag.

68
00:02:54,904 --> 00:02:58,328
Sorry, Noodle," I tell him.

69
00:02:58,328 --> 00:03:01,249
Your breakfast is in your bowl.

70
00:03:01,249 --> 00:03:04,633
He flicks his tail and walks away.

71
00:03:04,633 --> 00:03:06,644
Dad laughs.

72
00:03:06,644 --> 00:03:10,190
I think he wants to speak to the manager.
